  "readmeFile": "ReadMe.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 7.0.342\n\nFix: PollValues no longer silently swallows read errors - a failed poll now raises an error on the observable when no error handler is specified, #331880\n\nFix: PollValues releases its ADS variable handle on unsubscribe and recreates it after the target invalidated it (e.g. after a TwinCAT system restart), #331880\n\nVersion 7.0.276\n\nBreakingChange: SamplingManager is replaced by the mode-specific RawSamplingManager, RawFixedBufferSamplingManager, ValueSamplingManager and DynamicSamplingManager, all implementing ISamplingManager\n\nVersion 7.0.274\n\nEnh: SamplingManager and TypedSamplingManager share the common ISamplingManager interface (IsActive, InstancePath, DataType, IsTriggered, StoppedByCondition, Mode, StopSampling, Dispose); TypedSamplingManager gains the Mode and StoppedByCondition members\n\nVersion 7.0.272\n\nEnh: Added SamplingManager for cyclic polling of PLC symbols with configurable trigger, stop, and retrieval filter predicates. Supports typed sampling (by instance path or IValueSymbol) and raw byte sampling (by IndexGroup/IndexOffset).\n\nEnh: Added generic TypedSamplingManager<T> (where T : unmanaged) for high-performance, zero-boxing sampling of unmanaged PLC values. Subscribes to ADS notifications directly and reads each payload via MemoryMarshal.Read<T>, returning TypedSampleInfo<T> samples with strongly-typed Func<TypedSampleInfo<T>, bool> trigger/stop/retrieval predicates. Use SamplingManager for dynamic/string-filtered or structured values, and TypedSamplingManager<T> for primitive high-frequency access.\n\nVersion 7.0.109\n\nEnh: Fewer memory allocations and copy operations for better performance\n\nVersion 7.0.36\n\nBreakingChange: Removed the net6.0 target (.NET 6 is out of support)\n\nVersion 7.0\n\nEnh: Supports locally installed TwinCAT 2 (via PInvoke channel). The fallback to 'TcAmsServer.dll' also enables systems without an open TCP loopback port (e.g. TC2 or TCP loopback disabled), #230847\n\nEnh: Supports internal communication via UnixSockets, TCP/IP Loopback and PInvoke\n\nEnh: TargetFramework dependencies changed to net8.0, net6.0, netstandard2.0",
